// Constants.schema — the PROTOCOL ID's home, and it declares no table.
//
// This is the ordinary shape of a real unit and it is what the dogfood has:
// the constants live in their own file, that file sorts first, and
// `ir.ProtocolIdHome` therefore names a file with no `table` in it — a file
// that gets no Block source at all. A shared runtime emitted there would be
// emitted into a file nothing writes, and every reference to it undefined.
//
// The unit's shared C# runtime goes to <Package>Block.cs — BlockhomeBlock.cs,
// emitted for the UNIT because no file here is named for the package (§19.2).
// This file is here to make that a corpus fact rather than a claim.

package blockhome

const MaxParts  = 32
const MaxPlates = 4
